<title>NEW ZEALAND: No Forestry Corp buyback in coalition deal - Bolger.</title>
<headline>No Forestry Corp buyback in coalition deal - Bolger.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand Prime Minister Jim Bolger said on Wednesday the coalition deal his party struck with NZ First on Tuesday evening did not include any buy-back of Forestry Corporation.</p>
<p>The former state-owned corporation was sold in September for NZ$2 billion to a consortium led by Fletcher Challenge.</p>
<p>Bolger also said the coalition deal did not include a 25 percent limit on the level of foreign investment in New Zealand. NZ First campaigned in the run-up to the election to limit foreign investment and ownership in strategic assets, including utilities, to 24.9 percent.  </p>
<p>Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
